the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base annuity_full_surrender includes these resources:
    temporal.

the functions are:
    the effective date of *an activity* is *a date*.
    the account value of the policy before *an activity* is *an amount*.
    the issue date of the policy before *an activity* is *a date*.
    the duration of *an activity* is *a number*.
    the policy year of *an activity* is *a number*.
    the surrender charge rate of *an activity* is *a number*.
    the surrender charge of *an activity* is *an amount*.
    the surrender value of *an activity* is *an amount*.
    the account value of the policy after *an activity* is *a value*.
    the policy status of the policy after *an activity* is *a value*.

the templates are:
    *an activity* is a full surrender.
    the surrender charge rate for duration *a duration* is *a rate* under table surrender_charge.

the table surrender_charge is loaded from surrender_charge.csv, with unique match:
    duration | rate

the knowledge base annuity_full_surrender includes:

the text of "FullSurrender/Transaction.xml" is at "sources/FullSurrender/Transaction.xml".

% An activity of this program is a full surrender: the FullSurrender transaction it processes.
an activity is a full surrender if
    the effective date of the activity is a date.

rule duration with provenance "FullSurrender/Transaction.xml" at MathVariable DurationMV:
the duration of an activity is a number if
    the age on the effective date of the activity of someone born on the issue date of the policy before the activity is the number.

rule policy_year with provenance "FullSurrender/Transaction.xml" at MathVariable PolicyYearMV:
the policy year of an activity is a number N if
    the duration of the activity is a number M
    and N = M + 1.

rule surrender_charge_rate with provenance "FullSurrender/Transaction.xml" at MathVariable SurrenderChargeRateMV:
the surrender charge rate of an activity is a number N if
    the policy year of the activity is a second number
    and the surrender charge rate for duration the second number is N under table surrender_charge
    otherwise the activity is a full surrender
    and N = 0.

rule surrender_charge with provenance "FullSurrender/Transaction.xml" at MathVariable SurrenderChargeMV:
the surrender charge of an activity is an amount N if
    the account value of the policy before the activity is an amount M
    and the surrender charge rate of the activity is a number K
    and N = round(M * K * 100) / 100.

rule surrender_value with provenance "FullSurrender/Transaction.xml" at MathVariable SurrenderValueMV:
the surrender value of an activity is an amount N if
    the account value of the policy before the activity is an amount M
    and the surrender charge of the activity is an amount K
    and N = round((M - K) * 100) / 100.

rule copy_account_value with provenance "FullSurrender/CopyToPolicyFields.xml" at Field AccountValue:
the account value of the policy after an activity is 0 if
    the activity is a full surrender.

rule copy_policy_status with provenance "FullSurrender/CopyToPolicyFields.xml" at Field PolicyStatus:
the policy status of the policy after an activity is Surrendered if
    the activity is a full surrender.

scenario drained_w1_fullsurrender is:
    the effective date of w1_fullsurrender is 2022-07-01.
    the account value of the policy before w1_fullsurrender is 1500.
    the issue date of the policy before w1_fullsurrender is 2021-01-01.
    surrender_value expects answers ["the surrender value of w1_fullsurrender is 1410"].
    policy_after_account_value expects answers ["the account value of the policy after w1_fullsurrender is 0"].
    policy_after_policy_status expects answers ["the policy status of the policy after w1_fullsurrender is Surrendered"].

query surrender_value is:
    the surrender value of which activity is which amount.

query policy_after_account_value is:
    the account value of the policy after which activity is which value.

query policy_after_policy_status is:
    the policy status of the policy after which activity is which value.

the view full_surrender is:
    the title is "FullSurrender (annuity)".
    the case is a scenario.
    the facts about "the activity" are
        the effective date of an activity is a date.
    the facts about "the policy it finds" are
        the account value of the policy before an activity is an amount,
        the issue date of the policy before an activity is a date.
    the result is the answer to query surrender_value.
    the result shows its citations.

